### Sales Service – CRUD smoke tests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP client)
@host = http://localhost:4004
@svc  = {{host}}/odata/v4/sales

### 1. Read all Sales Orders
GET {{svc}}/SalesOrders

### 2. Read one order with its items (deep read)
GET {{svc}}/SalesOrders(11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111001)?$expand=Items

### 3. $search + $filter (what the List Report issues)
GET {{svc}}/SalesOrders?$search=Acme&$filter=Status eq 'Completed'&$orderby=OrderDate desc

### 4. DEEP INSERT – create an order together with its items in one call
# TotalAmount and each NetAmount are calculated by the service (don't send them).
POST {{svc}}/SalesOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "SalesOrderNo": "SO-2001",
  "CustomerID": "CUST-009",
  "CustomerName": "Wayne Enterprises",
  "OrderDate": "2026-06-01",
  "Status": "New",
  "Currency": "USD",
  "Items": [
    { "ItemNo": 10, "ProductID": "PROD-900", "ProductName": "Batmobile Tire", "Quantity": 4, "UnitPrice": 250.00, "Currency": "USD" },
    { "ItemNo": 20, "ProductID": "PROD-901", "ProductName": "Grappling Hook", "Quantity": 2, "UnitPrice": 120.00, "Currency": "USD" }
  ]
}

### 5. Validation – rejected because Quantity <= 0 (expect HTTP 400)
POST {{svc}}/SalesOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "SalesOrderNo": "SO-2002",
  "CustomerName": "Bad Qty Co",
  "Items": [ { "ItemNo": 10, "ProductID": "P1", "ProductName": "X", "Quantity": 0, "UnitPrice": 10 } ]
}

### 6. Validation – rejected because SalesOrderNo already exists (expect HTTP 400)
POST {{svc}}/SalesOrders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "SalesOrderNo": "SO-1001", "CustomerName": "Dup Co" }

### 7. Update a header field (PATCH)
PATCH {{svc}}/SalesOrders(11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111003)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "Status": "In Process" }

### 8. Delete an order (cascades to its items via composition)
DELETE {{svc}}/SalesOrders(11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111005)

### 9. Value-help collections
GET {{svc}}/OrderStatus
GET {{svc}}/Currencies
